ROCR: gfx11 retained-PM4 encoder supports enable_sgpr_dispatch_ptr.

Applies with -p1 at projects/rocr-runtime of rocm-10-sdk-pm4-prepared-source, AFTER Codex's
scratchless-preserve-tmpring.patch. Source of truth:
/mnt/Home/src/pm4-clr-gatelog/rocm-10-sdk-pm4-prepared-source, b499e3e..62d8310.

Torch kernels set kernel_code_properties 0x040a (dispatch ptr, kernarg segment ptr, wave32); the
encoder rejected every such kernel because it only supported bits 0, 3 and 10. Each command
list now owns a GPU-visible copy of its AQL packets (amd_graph_command_encoder.h,
hsa_ven_amd_graph.cpp) and the encoder passes the packet address in the dispatch-pointer user
SGPRs, in ABI order (private segment buffer, dispatch ptr, kernarg ptr).

